    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Incoming volunteers can read a short handover note and overlap with the outgoing team.\", \"decision\": \"How should the team prepare a fresh volunteer shift?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nBoth teams update the handover note during each transfer of a task in the overlap. The record follows the actual transfer of responsibility.\nThe outgoing team writes the handover note before the overlap and demonstrates the current work afterward. The incoming team can connect a prepared summary with the live process.\nThe incoming team watches the current work during the overlap and writes the handover note with the outgoing team. The note records what the new volunteers have just checked."
    }
